---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms — CITY JAM" description="The terms, in English. You keep your music." path="/terms">
  <header class="hero dark bg-deep">
    <div class="wrap narrow">
      <p class="kick"><span class="dot"></span> Terms · last updated 10 October 2026</p>
      <h1>The terms, in <em>English</em>.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Written to be read, not to be survived. If a clause here needs a lawyer to decode, that is our failure and we want to hear about it.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section>
    <div class="wrap narrow legal">
      <div class="note"><b>You keep your music. All of it.</b> We do not take a share of your masters, your publishing, or your rights by you filling in a form or following a link on this website. If we ever want a licence to anything, we will ask you, in a separate agreement, and you can say no.</div>
      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>CITY JAM (“we”, “us”) operates joinourjam.com and the CITY JAM magazine, playlists, app and related services. These terms govern your use of the website.</p>
      <p>The legal entity, the registered address, and the law that governs these terms are not settled in public. They will be named here before anything on this site takes money or asks you to rely on a contract. Until then, do not treat a country named in an old draft as the answer.</p>
      <h2>2. Using the site</h2>
      <p>You may read, listen, and follow the links to apply for the things we offer. You may not scrape the site, resell it, misrepresent yourself, or use it to harass anyone. If you are under 16, get a parent or guardian to agree to these terms with you.</p>
      <h2>3. Your music</h2>
      <p><b>Sending music to CITY JAM transfers nothing.</b> You keep every right you had before you sent it.</p>
      <p>What you give us, by submitting, is a narrow permission: to listen to it, internally, in order to consider it. That is the whole licence. It is non-exclusive, revocable, and it exists only so that pressing play is not an infringement.</p>
      <p>If we want to write about it, put it in a playlist, feature it in print, or use a clip, we ask you first and you can say no. Saying no does not affect how your next submission is judged.</p>
      <h2>4. What you promise us</h2>
      <p>That the music you send is yours to send. That it does not infringe anyone else’s rights. And that it is <b>not AI-generated</b>. We screen for this, and we will remove anything that fails.</p>
      <h2>5. Editorial independence</h2>
      <p>This is a term, not a marketing line. <b>Editorial coverage is not for sale.</b> Partners, advertisers, studios, brands and sponsors cannot buy a review, a score, a place on a list, or a sentence of editorial copy. Partner work is marked as partner work.</p>
      <h2>6. Money</h2>
      <p>This website does not take payment. There is no card form and no payment processor wired up. Where a page names a price, that price is the published offer, not a checkout. When a processor exists, it will be named here, and not before.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Creator Labs.</b> Applying takes a deposit, refunded in full whether or not we offer you a place. The amount is not stated because it is not settled. Nothing is charged on this website.</li>
        <li><b>Founders</b> is a one-time contribution, not a subscription, and never renews. It is not taken on this website.</li>
        <li><b>Nobody’s Looking</b> is a one-time purchase when it is for sale. It is not for sale from this page.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Your statutory cancellation rights need to be set out properly by a solicitor before anyone is charged. That clause is not pretended into existence here.</p>
      <h2>7. Things we cannot promise</h2>
      <p>That we will write about your music. That the app will do a specific thing by a specific date. That a booking, a partnership or a placement will happen. We will tell you honestly where things stand.</p>
      <h2>8. Ending it</h2>
      <p>You can stop using CITY JAM whenever you like and ask us to delete what we hold. We can suspend access that breaks these terms, and we will tell you why.</p>
      <h2>9. Liability</h2>
      <p>Nothing here limits liability that the law does not allow us to limit. Beyond that, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss.</p>
      <h2>10. Changes</h2>
      <p>If we change these terms materially, we will say what changed and why. Not a silent diff in a footer.</p>
      <h2>11. Talking to us</h2>
      <p><a href="mailto:hello@joinourjam.com">Write to us</a>. A person reads it.</p>
      <div class="acts">
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/">Back to the room</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
